The discovery of well-preserved dinosaur skin impressions has offered new insights into their outer appearance, including patterns and texture, which were previously unknown.	To'g'ri saqlangan dinozavrlarning teri izlari o'zlarining tashqi ko'rinishi, jumladan, nishonlar va qoplamalar haqida oldin ma'lum bo'lmagan yangi ma'lumotlar berdi.
Scientists believe the bird's feathers likely played a role in attracting mates, with vibrant coloration possibly used in courtship displays.	Scientistlar bu hayvonning qushlari jinsiy tanlovda ishtirok etish uchun yorqin ranglarga ega bo'lishi ehtimoli borligini taxmin qilishmoqda.
The discovery provides new evidence about how early dinosaurs may have used feathers for insulation rather than flight.	 Bu kashf, qadimgi dinosavrlarning qanotlarni uchish uchun emas, balki issiqlikni saqlash uchun qanday foydalanishini tushunishda yangi dalillar beradi.
The discovery suggests that feather-like structures may have evolved before the development of the central shaft, indicating that insulation or display functions could have preceded flight-related adaptations.	 Bu kashfiyot qo‘shimcha tayoqchalarning (rachis) rivojlanishidan oldin qo‘shimcha tayoqchalarning (barbs va barbules) mavjudligi, ya'ni issiqlik saqlash yoki ko'rinish funksiyalarining uchuvchilikka oid xususiyatlardan oldin rivojlanishini ko'rsatadi.
The discovery of well-preserved feathers in a juvenile dinosaur fossil indicates that some dinosaurs may have had complex feather patterns much earlier in life than previously thought.	Shu yoshdagi dinozavrlarning qoldiqlarida saqlangan qush poyasi topilishi, ba'zi dinozavrlarning hayotining juda yoshida murakkab poyali tuzilishga ega bo'lishi mumkinligini ko'rsatadi.
The discovery indicates that the dinosaur may have been fully feathered at birth, suggesting advanced developmental traits similar to modern birds.	Shu kashf, bu dinozavrlarning tug'ilganda to'liq qushlarga o'xshab qulay qilingan bo'lishi, modern qushlarga o'xshab murakkab rivojlanish xususiyatlarini ko'rsatadi.
