The World Health Organization has warned that the cholera outbreak in Haiti could worsen if sanitation conditions in the affected areas are not improved promptly.	 Xalqaro Sog‘liqni Saqlash Tashkiloti Haitadagi kolera pandemiyasining yaxshilanishiga yordam berish uchun afzal ravishda sozlash sharoitlari yaxshilanmasa, bu holat yaxshilanmay olishi haqida ogohlantirish berdi.
The contamination of the Artibonite River's tributary led to a severe outbreak of cholera in nearby communities, prompting widespread public health concerns.   Artibonite daryosining oqimiga nishonlanayotgan ifloslanish, ya'ni yaqin atrofdagi hududlarda koliqra virusi tarqotishiga sabab bo'ldi, bu esa keng ko'lamli sog'liqni saqlash muammolarini keltirib chiqardi.
Before the outbreak of the cholera epidemic in 2010, Haiti had not reported any major cases of the disease for over a century.   2010-yilda kolera epidemiyasidan oldin, Gaiti bir asrdan ortiq davomida katta hajmdagi kasalliklarni his qilmagan edi.
The World Health Organization has emphasized the importance of improving healthcare infrastructure in rural areas to prevent future disease outbreaks.	Birinchi jahon sog‘liqni saqlash tashkiloti qishloq hududlarida sog‘liqni saqlash infrastrukturasi yaxshilanishining kelajakdagi kasalliklarni oldini olish uchun ahamiyatini ta'kidladi.
Danielle Lantagne, the UN's disease expert, emphasized that the outbreak could have been triggered by contaminated water sources used by peacekeeping troops.   Danielle Lantagne, jihodga doir bo‘lgan Birlashgan Millatlar tashkiloti eksperti, epidemiyaga muntazam suv manbalari, shuningdek, xavfsizlik kuchlarining foydalanishiga olib kelgan bo‘lishi ehtimoli borligini ta'kidladi.
The hospital staff reported that the patient was transferred to a specialized care unit for further evaluation and treatment.	Bemor xavfsiz holatda bo‘lgani uchun bo‘shatilgan bo‘limga o‘tkazilganligi haqida xodimlar xabar berdi.
