On the morning of October 6, 1789, a large crowd of Parisian women, frustrated by food shortages, marched on Versailles and demanded that the royal family return to the capital to be closer to the people.   6-oktabr kuni ertalab, ovqat yetishmovchiligi tufayli xursand bo'lmagan Parijlik ayollar Versalliya qarab yurishdi va hukmdor oilasini aholi yaqinida bo'lishi uchun poytaxtga qaytishini talab qildi.
As the royal family arrived at the palace gates, they were met with silence, broken only by the distant sound of drums and the occasional cry from the crowd.	 Poytaxtga kelganda, ular o‘zlarini qo‘rqinchli xavfli aylanib olib, qo‘shni yig‘inlarning o‘ziga xos ovozlarini eshitishdi.
The crowd shouted demands for justice, pushing the royal couple to stand up in the carriage and face them directly.	Odamlar to'plami adolatni talab qilishdi va sultan va sultonga o'zlarini karavandda to'g'ridan-to'g'ri ularning oldiga chiqishga majbur qildi.
