Technological determinism is often criticized for oversimplifying the complex relationship between society and innovation, ignoring the role of cultural, political, and economic factors in shaping technological development.   Texnologik qat'iyat ko'pincha ijtimoiy taraqqiyot va innovatsiyalar o'rtasidagi murakkab munosabatlarni soddalashtirish uchun sharhlanadi va texnologik rivojlanishni shakllantiruvchi madaniy, siyosiy va iqtisodiy omillarni e'tiborsiz qoldiradi.
Technological determinism often assumes that innovations emerge from internal technological logic rather than from social needs or political decisions.	Texnologik qat'iyatga ko'ra, innovatsiyalar ijtimoiy ehtiyojlardan yoki siyosiy qarorlardan emas, balki ichki texnologik mantiqdan kelib chiqadi.
