Subcultures often provide a supportive environment where individuals can express their unique interests and values without fear of judgment.	Subkulturlar odatda odamlarga ijodiy qiziqishlari va qiymatlarini boshqalarning qiyosiga qaramay, xavfsizlik bilan ifodalash imkonini beradi.
Subcultures often emerge as a response to mainstream societal norms, offering alternative values, styles, and forms of expression.	Subkulturlar ko'pincha asosiy jamiyat normalariga javob sifatida paydo bo'lib, almashtirilgan qiymatlar, uslublar va ifoda shakllarini taklif qiladi.
Subcultures often emerge in response to mainstream societal norms, reflecting shared values, behaviors, and identities among specific groups.	Subkulturlar ko'pincha asosiy jamiyat normalariga javob sifatida paydo bo'ladi va ma'lum guruhlarning birgalikdagi qiymatlarini, harakatlarini va identifikatsiyasini aks ettiradi.
In many subcultures, shared music preferences serve as a powerful indicator of identity and belonging.	 Ko'plab subkulturning a'zolari o'zlarining identiteti va qo'shni bo'lishi haqida ma'lumot berish uchun bir xil musiqa sevimlari bilan ifodalashadi.
One of the key reasons researchers study feral children is to understand the critical role of early social interaction in human development.	Yetkazilgan bolalar haqida tadqiqotlar olib borishning asosiy sabablari orasida inson rivojlanishida early ijtimoiy aloqaning muhim ahamiyati haqida tushuncha egallash hisoblanadi.
These children often struggle to develop language and social skills, even after being rescued and placed in supportive environments.	Shu bolalar odatda til va ijtimoiy ko'nikmalarni rivojlantirishda qiyinchiliklar bilan duch keladi, hatto qutqarilgan va qo'llab-quvvatlovchi muhitga joylashtirilgandan so'ng ham.
Children who grow up in extreme isolation often struggle with basic social skills and language development, even when they are later reintegrated into society.   Boshqarilmaslikda o'sgan bolalar, ular keyin jamiyatga qaytib qo‘shilganda ham asosiy ijtimoiy ko'nikmalar va til rivojlanishida qiyinchiliklarga duch keladi.
Some of these individuals were reportedly raised in isolation from human society, with limited or no contact with people during their early years.   Ushbu shaxslarning ba'zilari o‘zining yoshlik yillarida inson jamoasidan izolyatsiyada, odamlar bilan cheklangan yoki hech qanday aloqasi bo‘lmagan holda tarbiyalanganligi aytiladi.
When raised exclusively by animals, feral children often display social and emotional behaviors that closely mirror those of their animal caregivers, including a lack of interest in human interaction or communication.	 Hayvonlar tomonidan butunlay tarbiyalangan feral bolalar o'zlarining hayvoniy tarbiyachilari bilan bir xil ijtimoiy va emotsional xatti-harakatlarni ko'rsatadilar, jumladan, insonlarga qiziqish yoki aloqaga ega bo'lmaganlik.
Scaffolding provides temporary support to students as they develop new skills, gradually reducing assistance as independence grows.   Sillablar o‘quvchilarga yangi ko‘nikmalarni rivojlantirishda vaqti-vaqti bilan yordam beradi, mustaqillik oshganda yordamni kamaytiradi.
Scaffolding is a temporary support structure used in education to help learners gradually build their understanding and skills until they can perform tasks independently.   Ta'limda scaffolding — o'quvchilarning mustaqil ravishda vazifalarni bajarishiga qadar tushunish va ko'nikmalarni rivojlantirishiga yordam beradigan vaqtinchalik yordam tizimi hisoblanadi.
A well-designed classroom environment can act as a scaffold by providing visual cues, structured routines, and clear expectations to support student learning.	To'g'ri dizayn qilingan dars xonasining o'quvchilarning o'rganishiga yordam berish uchun vizual ko'rsatgichlar, tuzilgan jarayonlar va aniq kutilayotgan natijalar berishi mumkin.
Virtual Scaffolds are integrated into educational software to guide learners through complex tasks by providing step-by-step support and interactive feedback.   Virtual Scaffolds ta'lim dasturlariga integratsiyalangan bo'lib, o'quvchilarga murakkab vazifalarni bajarishda bosqichma-bosqich yordam berish va interaktiv foydalanishni ta'minlaydi.
Children in foster care often face emotional and psychological challenges due to their traumatic experiences before placement.	Taxminan qo‘shimcha o‘rnatilgan bolalar o‘zlarining joylashtirilishidan oldin tug‘ilgan traumalari tufayli ruhiy va psixologik qiyinchiliklarga duch keladi.
Every child deserves a safe and supportive environment where they can learn, thrive, and develop their full potential, yet millions still face adversity and neglect.	Barcha bolalarga o‘zining to‘liq potensialini rivojlantirish, o‘rganish va rivojlanish uchun xavfsiz va qo‘llab-quvvatlash muhitida yashash huquqi bo‘lishi kerak, lekin millionlab bolalar hali ham qiyinchiliklar va e'tiborsizlikka duch kelmoqda.
The government has launched a new initiative to improve foster care conditions and provide better support for children in the system.   Hukumat foster care sharoitlarini yaxshilash va tizimda bo‘lgan bolalarga yaxshiroq yordam ko‘rsatish uchun yangi dasturni boshladi.
The system aims to support children in transitioning smoothly into independent adulthood with access to counseling, job training, and long-term social services.	Tizim o‘zini o‘ziga qo‘shilishda yordam berish, ishga joylashtirish tayyorgarligi va uzoq muddatli ijtimoiy xizmatlarga kirish imkonini berish maqsadini qo‘ygan.
Children in foster care are entitled to receive regular medical check-ups, educational support, and emotional counseling to ensure their overall well-being.   Foster o‘quvchilarga ularning umumiy rivojlanishini ta'minlash uchun doimiy tibbiy tekshiruvlar, ta'lim yordami va psixologik yordam berilishiga haq qo‘shiladi.
