Scientific progress relies not only on experiments but also on careful data analysis, peer review, and the ability to revise theories in light of new evidence.	Scientifik ilg‘orlik faqat tajribalarga emas, balki ma’lumotlarni e’tiborli tahlil qilishga, mutaxassislarning sharhini olishga hamda yangi dalillar asosida nazariyalarni takomillashtirish qobiliyatiga ham bog‘liq.
During the Renaissance, scholars began to rediscover ancient Greek and Roman works, translating them from Greek and Latin into vernacular languages for wider understanding.	Renessans davrida olimlar qadimgi Yaxshilik va Rim asarlari o‘zlarini g‘oyat yaxshi tushunish uchun ularni yunon va lotin tilidan o‘zining o‘ziga xos tiliga tarjima qilishni boshladilar.
In medieval times, Aristotelian philosophy dominated academic thought, particularly in the fields of ethics and natural philosophy.	 O'rta asrlarda, Aristotel filosofiyasi axloq va tabiiy filosofiya sohalarida ilmiy fikrlashni boshqaradi.
As the influence of classical learning waned in Europe, scholars increasingly turned to Arabic translations of ancient texts for insight into Greek philosophy and science.   Yevropada klassik o‘quv yozuvlarning ta'siri kamayganda, olimlar qadimgi yunon filosofiyasi va faniga oid tushunchalarni olish uchun aralik tilidagi qadimgi matnlarga kengroq murojaat qilishni boshladilar.
