This allows them to exploit a greater variety of microhabitats for shelter and protection against natural enemies.   Bu ularning tabiiy enemylardan himoya qilish uchun ko'proq mikrohabitatlardan foydalanish imkonini beradi.
While most insects have the ability to fold their wings when at rest, only dragonflies and mayflies retain the unique trait of keeping their wings extended permanently.   Barcha insectlar uchun nafas olish vaqti o‘zlarining qanotlarini qisqartirish qobiliyati mavjud bo‘lsa ham, faqat baliqlar va mayflylar o‘zlarining qanotlarini doimiy ravishda keng qilish xususiyatiga ega bo‘lishadi.
Around 2,300 years ago, the ancient Greek astronomer Hipparchus developed one of the first comprehensive star catalogs, laying the foundation for future celestial mapping.   2,300 yil oldin, qadimgi yunon astronomi Gipparx birinchi keng qamrovli yulduzlar katalogini ishlab chiqdi, keyingi yulduzlar xaritalashish uchun asos qo‘ydi.
Many ancient astronomers, such as Ptolemy, supported the geocentric model, arguing that Earth was the stationary center of the universe, with all celestial bodies revolving around it.   Ko'plab qadimgi astronomlar, jumladan, Ptolemei, geotsentrik modelni qo'llab-quvvatlagan bo'lib, Yer universumning harakatsiz markazi bo'lib, barcha ashtoq jismlar uning atrofida aylanayotganini ishonishgan.
