The Amazon River's vast basin plays a crucial role in regulating the global climate by storing massive amounts of carbon dioxide.	Amazon daryosining katta havzasi global iqlimni karbon qaytarish gazini saqlash orqali iqlimni nazorat qilishda muhim rol o'ynaydi.
The Amazon River is not only the largest by volume but also flows through nine countries in South America, supporting a vast and diverse ecosystem.   Amazon daryosi hajmi bo‘yicha eng katta bo‘lib, shuningdek, Janubiy Amerikada to'rtto'rtta mamlakatdan o'tib oqadi va keng ko'lamli, turli xil ekotizimni qo'llab-quvvatlaydi.
The Amazon River contributes more than half of the freshwater entering the Atlantic Ocean each year.   Yiliga Atlantika okeaniga suv oqimining yarimidan ortig‘i Amazon daryosidan keladi.
The Amazon River basin spans over 7 million square kilometers, making it the largest drainage basin in the world.   Amazon daryosi havzasi 7 million kvadrat kilometrdan ortiq maydonni qamrab oladi va bu jahonning eng katta suv oqimini yig‘uvchi havzadir.
